<pre class=metadata>
Title: Form Factor Media Query
Shortname: form-factor-media-query
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/form-factor/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification adds the '@media/form-factor' media feature, which reports the kind of device the
    page is shown on, from a closed list: a desktop computer, a phone, a tablet, a television, a watch, a
    headset, an e-ink reader, or a car. Media queries already describe what a device can do, and a page can
    often guess from that, but the guesses are wrong in the cases that matter, and nothing distinguishes a
    television from a laptop. The feature matches the form factors of the User-Agent Client Hint of the same
    name, is limited in cross-origin frames by the same policy that delegates that hint, and falls back to the
    coarse mobile signal that every site already receives where fingerprinting protections apply.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
